 "answer": "Use **`pg_relation_size()`** on the index name, wrapped in `pg_size_pretty()` for readability:\n\n```sql\nSELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size('my_vector_index'));\n```\n\npgvector's HNSW and IVFFlat indexes are ordinary Postgres index access methods, so the standard size functions work on them. `pg_relation_size()` returns the size of the main fork, which is the index data itself. To include the free space map and visibility map, use `pg_table_size()` or `pg_total_relation_size()` instead. To get the combined size of all indexes on a table, use `pg_indexes_size('my_table')`.",
